> If you like unambiguous forms, use the full form of the gismu and
> separate them with "zei" ('lujvo glue'), which is for lujvo based on
> words that don't have rafsi.   
> E.g., lojbau (Lojban + language) = lojbo zei bangu.  This way you
> don't have to remember any rafsi. 

Though you can also use four-letter rafsi for all but the final
component and use the full gismu for that: "lojbybangu", which also
means the same thing. And it shouldn't be too hard to remember the
four-letter ones :)

